      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To find the value of $(2x + 5)^2$ when $x$ equals 3, we will substitute the given value into the expression and simplify it step by step. Here's the reasoning:\n\n1. **Substitute \\( x = 3 \\) into the expression \\( 2x + 5 \\):**\n   \\[\n   2(3) + 5\n   \\]\n\n2. **Calculate the multiplication:**\n   \\[\n   2 \\times 3 = 6\n   \\]\n   So, the expression becomes:\n   \\[\n   6 + 5\n   \\]\n\n3. **Perform the addition:**\n   \\[\n   6 + 5 = 11\n   \\]\n\n4. **Now, square the result:**\n   \\[\n   (2x + 5)^2 = 11^2\n   \\]\n\n5. **Calculate the square:**\n   \\[\n   11^2 = 11 \\times 11\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   11 \\times 11 = 121\n   \\]\n\nThus, the value of $(2x + 5)^2$ when \\( x = 3 \\) is \\(\\boxed{121}\\).",
